From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:17:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Use the Modrinth Enhanced icon

Replaces the bundled application icons with the Modrinth mark on a deep
green disc, plus a sparkle badge marking the build as the enhanced fork.

The disc is green rather than near-black: against a dark taskbar an
almost-black circle has no silhouette at all, which is what made the
icon hard to pick out.

Two vector sources are checked in next to the generated files.
`modrinth-enhanced.svg` is used from 64px up. Below that the mark's rings
fall under a pixel and smear together, so `modrinth-enhanced-small.svg`
scales the mark past the edge of the disc, keeping a shape that still
reads at 16px. scripts/render-icons.py regenerates the set from both.

`icons/apple.icon` is left untouched: it is an Icon Composer source that
nothing in the build references.
